"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:20f1d495cf8199324f0ca9bd2a7523ebc505a6b7582768db786db10ddc046265","file":"preprints/The-trace-cone-classifies-Razak-Jacelon-stabilizations-September-25-2026/build/sections/02-structure.tex","line":156,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"b4506bf44087fb269e559f8d44c62df776d8d414fbb1136034183a8de8fa8a41","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-trace-cone-classifies-Razak-Jacelon-stabilizations-September-25-2026/build/sections/02-structure.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:20f1d495cf8199324f0ca9bd2a7523ebc505a6b7582768db786db10ddc046265","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-trace-cone-classifies-Razak-Jacelon-stabilizations-September-25-2026/build/sections/02-structure.tex#L156"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{st:ideals}\nThe maps \\(F,G\\) identify the complete ideal lattices of \\(P\\) and\n\\(Q\\), and these identifications agree. They identify the finite\nand zero ideals of corresponding weights. The resulting\nhomeomorphism of primitive ideal spaces will be used to regard\n\\(\\Prim(P)=\\Prim(Q)=X\\). For an open \\(U\\subseteq X\\), write\n\\(P(U)\\) and \\(Q(U)\\) for the corresponding ideals. Then\n\\[\n G(\\Cu(P(U)))=\\Cu(Q(U)),\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n \\Fin(\\tau)=Q(U)\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\Fin(F\\tau)=P(U),\n \\qquad\n \\Ker(\\tau)=Q(U)\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\Ker(F\\tau)=P(U).\n\\]"}
